      "title": "Changelog",
      "body": "Below, we will keep track of all the changes made over the lifetime of this document. This way, all our members can see how the documents are changing over time.\n\nJanuary - 2026 (V. 26.1) Formatting redone for consistency and legibility. Except points listed below, no content changes.\n\nReplace:\nThroughout the document “Buhurt “Optimized” Eye bars” by “Safety Eye bars”\n\nAdd? “1. Implementation” (and subsequent modification of all Title numbers in the document) Clarification:\n\n- Split of “1. Definition and general requirements” in “2. Definition and description” and “3. General Requirements”. This split doesn’t have an impact on the content of the rules.\n\nAdd:\n\n- 2.2 Eye bars description: whole paragraph on Integrated Eye bars and multiple precisions on Externally riveted Eye bars and Safety Eye bars\n\nAdd: “5. Integrated Eye bars” (and subsequent modification of all Title numbers in the document) Replace:\n\n- In 5.1 Historical Sources and Datation: “The main source is the Great Helm from Nuremberg (1350).” by “One artifact from the Churburg castle shows a nice example.”\n\n- In 6.4 Examples of Denied Reproductions: “Too much eyebars” by “too many Eye bars”\n\nDecember-2024: -add Document has been created",
